The graph below shows a cubic polynomial with leading coefficient $1$. Which is its equation?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw[<->] (-6.6,0)--(8,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[<->] (0,-3.4)--(0,3.4) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[thick,blue,<->,domain=-5.85:7.23,smooth,variable=\x,samples=60] plot ({\x},{0.038*(\x+5)*(\x-2)*(\x-6)});
\fill (-5,0) circle (2pt);
\node[below left] at (-5,0) {$(-5,0)$};
\fill (2,0) circle (2pt);
\node[below left] at (2,0) {$(2,0)$};
\fill (6,0) circle (2pt);
\node[below right] at (6,0) {$(6,0)$};
\fill (0,2.28) circle (2pt);
\node[above right] at (0,2.28) {$(0,60)$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

The graph below shows a cubic polynomial $y=P(x)$. Which is the correct **form** of its equation?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw[<->] (-6.6,0)--(2.8,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[<->] (0,-3.4)--(0,3.4) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[thick,blue,<->,domain=-6.0:1.87,smooth,variable=\x] plot ({\x},{0.10*(\x+4)*(\x+4)*(\x-1)});
\fill (-4,0) circle (2pt);
\node[above left] at (-4,0) {$(-4,0)$};
\fill (1,0) circle (2pt);
\node[above right] at (1,0) {$(1,0)$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

The cubic graphed below has equation $y=k(x+2)(x-1)(x-4)$. Find $k$.
