The quartic graphed below has equation $y=k(x+1)^{2}(x-3)^{2}$. Find its equation.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw[<->] (-2.8,0)--(4.8,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[<->] (0,-3.4)--(0,1)  node[above] {$y$};
\draw[thick,blue,<->,domain=-2.08:4.07,smooth,variable=\x,samples=60] plot ({\x},{-0.10*(\x+1)*(\x+1)*(\x-3)*(\x-3)});
\fill (-1,0) circle (2pt);
\node[above left] at (-1,0) {$(-1,0)$};
\fill (3,0) circle (2pt);
\node[above right] at (3,0) {$(3,0)$};
\fill (1,-1.6) circle (2pt);
\node[below right] at (1,-1.6) {$(1,-16)$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
